save.description:
This is a warning, not a refusal — an installation may deliberately be set up in an unusual way, and only you know whether it is.

{problems}

The same list appears under Repairs for as long as it applies.

invalid_config.description:
{count} problem(s) were found in this installation. The zones that are sound carry on being regulated; the rest stand down until this is fixed.

{problems}

Open the integration and choose Configure to correct them. The full list is in the downloadable diagnostics.

manual_sources.description:
{count} duty(ies) can only be delivered by a source with automatic start off, so they never start by themselves:

{problems}

That may be exactly what you want - a unit you switch on yourself is a fine choice. Confirm this notice once and it stays away, even after a restart. If you would rather the director drive these duties too, open the integration, choose Configure and switch automatic start on for one source.

unsupported_modes.description:
These appliances have a role that can ask for a mode they do not report - for example cooling on a unit that only knows `heat` and `off`. The director skips them for that mode, so the zone silently does nothing.

{entities}

Check the role under Configure, or the appliance's `hvac_modes` under Developer tools. This notice disappears by itself once every appliance reports the modes its role may ask for.

command_not_taking.description:
The director has been asking these appliances for the same thing for a while, and they keep reporting something else - the call is accepted and nothing happens, or the appliance puts itself straight back:

{entities}

For as long as that lasts the same call goes out again every round, some fourteen hundred a day, and nowhere is anything of it to be seen. Check the appliance under Developer tools: is it reachable, does it accept the mode, and is something else putting it back - a thermostat schedule, another automation? This notice disappears by itself once the appliance follows its command.
